            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Malayalam for a sculptor, then the Malayalam for an exhibition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: കച്ചേരി",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കച്ചേരി — kaccēri — \"a concert; a recital\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ഇന്നലെ രാത്രി ഞങ്ങൾ ഒരു സംഗീത കച്ചേരിക്ക് പോയി. innale rātri ñaṅṅaḷ oru saṁgīta kaccērikkŭ pōyi. Last night we went to a music concert."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A classical concert; the same word also names a court or a government office."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "കച്ചേരി (kaccēri) is usually traced to the North Indian word for a court-house, Hindi kacaharī, which CDIAL sets under a reconstructed compound meaning court-house (CDIAL 3429). Malayalam keeps the sense of a court or an office; how it came to mean a concert is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
